But I disagree with your “foul” pronouncement, as IMO the clue for “true leaves” already *does* give you a strong hint that the answer might be a more specialized term than “tree leaves”. And even if that term is totally new to you (as it was to me), I’d argue that it is deducible enough. Also: it’s Saturday :)

@Anonymous

Fair enough. Totally agree re Saturday. And I tried to indicate I wasn’t in too much of a snit about it. I mainly wanted to suggest how I thought a bit of editing could have helped with an area that legitimately created problems beyond what I consider IMO to be the usual challenges of devilish wordplay or appropriate obscurity — without either sacrificing the fill or dumbing down the puzzle. Indeed I think using “cotyledons” in the clue would have been MORE Saturday-worthy (“what the hell are cotyledons?” I imagine many posters complaining) than the actual clue. 

But of course hindsight is a tie vote, as I learned in yesterday’s puzzle.

@Barry Ancona

Good point re: tree leaves and green paint (a definition I don't always like). At the time, I plunked it in without much thought – but it is what caused me to get the Almost There message! 

For me, getting to CUREL was yet another reminder that – no matter how devious – setters want solvers to be able to complete their puzzles. So in this case, I need to question the inner voice that tells me with a shrug "Cerel must be some esoteric brand," when in fact I've seen it in the drugstore for ages. @NatK, perhaps that was the clue that could have used some gentle editing!

@Charlotte K
